  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The given conformation are of the following compound\r\n\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/BkNxOIAtxhe0FIUxcm3-iSohhglpAkYs5r8ywpE7uLM.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\r\n\r\nNote : Fisher conformation always show the eclipsed form of molecule. Thus, we have to convert the given staggered conformation of 'O' to an eclipsed conformation.<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/H1wE3LQDmoqiPus0uIrgTvx5VJLVxkBs1cKkYXYVYaM.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\r\n\r\nBased on the above structures, we can say that\r\n\r\n(a) $\\mathrm{M}$ and $\\mathrm{N}$ are diastereomers or non-mirror image stereoisomers.\r\n\r\n(b) $\\mathrm{M}$ and $\\mathrm{O}$ are identical.\r\n\r\n(c) $\\mathrm{M}$ and $\\mathrm{P}$ are enantiomers.\r\n\r\n(d) $\\mathrm{M}$ and $\\mathrm{Q}$ are diastereomers and therefore not identical.",
